{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "City of Evil combines melodic metal with energetic guitar work, which feels like a natural next choice after my In Flames albums.",
    "One-X matches the heavy, melodic rock I enjoy in One Day Remains and Ten Thousand Fists, while Mezmerize offers the aggressive riffs and unusual rhythms that appeal to me in Disturbed and Tool."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Stadium Arcadium's funkier rock and 21st Century Breakdown's punk rock feel less suited to my current interest in heavier, guitar-driven music.",
    "I could not confidently identify Iv or Circus from their titles, so I passed because I lacked enough information to judge their fit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat a broad interest in rock as enough, although the weight of the riffs and the style of the music matter to me.",
    "Darkness or intensity alone does not make an album my first choice: Year Zero interests me, but I want guitar-driven metal more today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated In Flames choices suggest that the combination of heaviness, melody, and energetic guitars deserves more emphasis.",
    "An album can fit my taste without being something I choose this visit: Glorious Burden and Audioslave appealed to me, but I prioritized other albums and had picked enough."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in heavy music but sometimes stretched that interest into rock styles that do not match what I want right now."
}"}
